{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/539474-2e-frenzy-question-insults","id":539474,"title":"[2E] Frenzy Question: Insults?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-04T06:22:18-07:00","id":539474,"title":"[2E] Frenzy Question: Insults?","content":"So I didn't get into Vampire until Blood &amp; Smoke/2E. Like, at all, except for V:TM - Bloodlines back in the day (and every couple of years when I want to play a great game). So when I started running a 2E game, I read through the Frenzy rules and thought I had them down.<br /> <br /> However, some more vampire-savvy friends were asking me about why, when they called a bunch of vampires in a room vermin, nobody frenzied. I stared at them like they were asking why it rains sometimes and said, &quot;Because vampires aren't going to Frenzy just because you're a dick?&quot;<br /> <br /> Except when I read through the book again, and noticed a couple of lines &quot;Insulted by a superior&quot; and &quot;Insulted by an inferior&quot;. Which seems to back up his assertion that insults provoke Frenzy. If so, then I've been running my games wrong*. In my defense, the book is very shallow about what provokes Frenzy. It's: &quot;When the vampire faces danger, hunger, or threat&quot;. And then later for situational modifiers &quot;if the vampire's rival has made a point of goading her every time they meet, it may impose an additional -1 die penalty to the roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">*: Just kidding, there's no such thing as running a game wrong. But I'll still feel like I've got egg on my face.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T06:54:29-07:00","id":539506,"title":"","content":"I think it would depend on the insult. Personally, I wouldn't call for a frenzy check for simple namecalling (maybe if it's a deeply offensive slur). It's got to be something that seriously degrades, humiliates, or enrages the character to count for a Fenzy check in my opinion, and what kind of insult triggers that is going to be different for each character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T07:08:49-07:00","id":539512,"title":"","content":"&quot;If someone called you that, you'd want to punch them&quot; seems an appropriate metric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T08:22:43-07:00","id":539574,"title":"","content":"I usually use the players as a reaction standard. If insulting dialog is exchanged and the other players smirk, laugh, or otherwise react to an exchange than I'll consider requiring frenzy checks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T08:44:22-07:00","id":539596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/539474-2e-frenzy-question-insults?p=539574#post539574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually use the players as a reaction standard. If insulting dialog is exchanged and the other players smirk, laugh, or otherwise react to an exchange than I'll consider requiring frenzy checks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a strange ruling. Is that so that you can maintain tone or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T09:06:31-07:00","id":539623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/539474-2e-frenzy-question-insults?p=539596#post539596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems like a strange ruling. Is that so that you can maintain tone or what?</div> </div> </div> </div> To gauge reaction. If another player reacts it means that they thought it was a 'good' insult. Part of the frenzy check is embarrassment, the shame of being looked down on or laughed at. In some situations rather than abstracting that I use the people at the table to consider if an overly emotional response might be triggered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T11:49:45-07:00","id":539770,"title":"","content":"If a vampire fenzied every time someone insulted them, there would be no harpies - far too dangerous of a job. Trading insults is something that all vampires would do. There has to be some limit, or just every offhand remark would set them off, and that is just something I don't think is appropriate.<br /> <br /> I agree with most others here - if you want to trigger a frenzy from an insult, then it should be something that's dramatically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:27:56-07:00","id":540076,"title":"","content":"With a few exceptions the frenzy triggers are left up to the discretion of the ST, with input from the player. Being insulted or embarrassed isn't a hard and fast thing. It varies depending on individuals and circumstances.<br /> <br /> If you want to model goading someone into frenzy mechanically, you could use extended social actions (Charisma+Intimidation/Persuasion, minus target's Composure). Each roll is a turn of hurling insults. When you accumulate the target's Resolve (maybe Willpower if you want it to be more difficult to accomplish) in successes, they roll to resist frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T15:51:41-07:00","id":540094,"title":"","content":"Composure would seem the more appropriate metric here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:00:34-07:00","id":540103,"title":"","content":"That was my initial thought, but I found it a little wonky to stack both the defense and success threshold on Composure alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:01:05-07:00","id":540104,"title":"","content":"There's definitely a willpower component in keeping a leash on the Beast, thus the Resolve or even Willpower component.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T16:40:58-07:00","id":540160,"title":"","content":"I'd just handle it with Social Maneuvering, with the goal being to make the mark Frenzy. Insulting them outright would be forcing doors, while trying to subtly goad them would be normal Social Maneuvering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:01:50-07:00","id":540172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/539474-2e-frenzy-question-insults?p=540160#post540160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just handle it with Social Maneuvering, with the goal being to make the mark Frenzy. Insulting them outright would be forcing doors, while trying to subtly goad them would be normal Social Maneuvering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like Social Maneuvering for frenzy goading for a few reasons. <br /> <br /> It's set up to persuade someone to do something. That's not really what needling someone till they flip their shit is, so it's odd to represent it that way. The main issue is impression setting the time per roll. You're not trying to push someone to snap over the course of days or weeks. It could work with some modification, but I like an extended action as a model of what's happening in absence of a more complex tweak of SM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T17:50:27-07:00","id":540217,"title":"","content":"Well that's why an insult would be done with Forcing Doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:00:49-07:00","id":540246,"title":"","content":"The forcing doors part I can see, I suppose. <br /> <br /> Spending weeks subtly nudging someone into frenzy is weird. I can see it in certain cases but overall it feels odd. <br /> <br /> I get how it could be described, but, meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:08:36-07:00","id":540256,"title":"","content":"Makes perfect sense to me. You do little things to help build to the conclusion of sending them into frenzy. Your perfectly orchestrated plan to embarass them. Cackle as applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:15:04-07:00","id":540265,"title":"","content":"Yeah, standard social maneuvering would be subtly manipulating them into a situation to be publicly humiliated (which is a <i>very</i> vampire thing to do). Doesn't work real well if they don't have a good impression of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:18:31-07:00","id":540267,"title":"","content":"The hitch I'm having with the non-force method is Social Maneuvering assumes all direct (or at least a hell of a lot of direct) contact on your part. The subtly setting up situations thing can (and in most cases probably would) be done without any direct contact with the victim. <br /> <br /> It's close enough that it works, and you can file the system down for indirect cases at least. <br /> <br /> Okay, I'm bought in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T18:50:24-07:00","id":540339,"title":"","content":"No, you had it right. An appropriate insult would be throwing a drink in someone's face. If you are strictly talking about words then go with the &quot;fighting words&quot; standard, &quot;<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">those that by their very utterance inflict injury or tend to incite an immediate breach of the peace.&quot; The insult has to actually provoke the vampire, and would even if there was no beast. The beast steps in, or tries, to deal with the situation. The beast affects the reaction to stimuli, not the perception of it. The beast doesn't make a vampire get angry easier, it makes the vampire react worse, when the vampire would normally deal with stress like anger, fear, or hunger.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T19:38:45-07:00","id":540392,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for the long term social maneuvering example, I'd imagine a scene like you see in a lot of movies or shows about bullying, sorta like Carry. Imagine, there's people being nice to you to maneuver you into a situation. They hang out with you one time. Kiss you another time. Invite you to prom together. Then, right when you're at the prom and your defenses are down, they humiliate you in front of everyone. Cue frenzy. <br /> <br /> Could be a fun use of it, especially if your intention is to double cross that person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T06:53:33-07:00","id":541095,"title":"","content":"What others have said, it needs to be a serious insult. A slap in the face, in public, from a loved one. Being dressed down in front of your superiors. A drink in the face. Being spit upon. So on and so forth. Just calling someone a name like 'vermin', while irritating, won't provoke the Beast. The key issue here is dramatic timing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:02:14-07:00","id":543332,"title":"","content":"Culture probably plays an important role in this. Your average internet junkie casually wades through more insults in a day that his parents have in their entire life, but insult a Russian's mother and shit is going to hit the fan. Either way the insults need to be meaningful and have power.<br /> <br /> A vampire who just executed a perfect political coup against a rival is not going to flop into Frenzy the moment that rival starts spewing insults at the realization.<br /> They are going to enjoy their victory like the smug bastard they are, because those insults no longer have any power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T19:05:27-07:00","id":543334,"title":"","content":"Still, I'd bet there's one thing they could say that might set them off. You could probably use Auspex to find out what it was.<br /> <br /> Rambling insults can be ignored though, sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T02:09:13-07:00","id":543639,"title":"","content":"Catch someone in the right mood and just about anything would set a vampire off. The chart says it lists things that &quot;could&quot; provoke depending on the circumstances of the situation, makes it difficult to find the &quot;magic phrase&quot; to invoke a frenzy roll at any time. It shouldn't be too difficult to provoke a vampire if that is your intention, at least enough to force a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:59:09-07:00","id":544116,"title":"","content":"Which could be modeled as an empathy roll, which would be further incentive for Harpies to purchase that skill. Knowing the right thing to say, followed by saying it perfectly, followed by resisting it. Three rolls, three possibilities of failure. Hardly a one-hit kill but sufficiently laid out to count as a 'technique'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:15:29-07:00","id":544130,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to why your friend would want to force frenzy on a bunch of other vampires. Humiliating a few forcing them to band together against you o.O?<br /> <br /> Anyway no ones mentioned the bloodline Spina from the invicitus(p170) which represents the extreme of this conversation i think it would be a good read for OP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:23:25-07:00","id":544140,"title":"","content":"I love Spina. I really hope we'll get to see a blog post on them after Secrets of the Covenants comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:15:11-07:00","id":545201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/539474-2e-frenzy-question-insults?p=544140#post544140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Spina. I really hope we'll get to see a blog post on them after Secrets of the Covenants comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div> DaveH said he was thinking about making them into a bloodline again, IIRC. So....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T12:17:58-07:00","id":545616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/539474-2e-frenzy-question-insults?p=545201#post545201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> DaveH said he was thinking about making them into a bloodline again, IIRC. So....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he said his plan was to write them up in a blog post and that their Bloodline Gifts would specifically synergize with the Coutrsie fighting style in SotC. But I know the OP staff is small and very busy and don't always have time to post things like that, so I'm keeping my fingers crossed that they'll have time to post it not too long after SotC comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T10:03:47-07:00","id":548865,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone =D<br /> <br /> I have no idea about Spina, but here is my two cents.<br /> <br /> I agree with most people here (no actual experience with 2E stuff, have just read through it). The Social Maneuvering seems to fit for most of these situations. I also agree with nofather and Diggs. I'm sure there are certain times or certain phrases that would set someone off. Certain racial slurs. Example: With the 'vermin&quot; comment. I'm sure if that was said to certain Ventrue, or even a Nos who has tried his entire undead life to be above the norm. To not be a bottom feeder, having to hide from his prey, would be highly offended by that comment almost to the point of frenzy. I would argue that it is very situational. What is said, to whom, that characters background and there current state of mind. Someone who is already having a shit day, pissed off for most of it. Gets called something that he tries so dearly not to be, I would say he would need to spend a willpower to not frenzy at that point. But, I still like the social maneuvering for more subtle situations.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}